# --no-color (TUI-DESIGN-3 §3.2 twins): colour depth 0 turns the sweep off — the reveal still runs (its head `▓▒░` is a cell change), the
# mark is committed, and the 12 s alone write zero frames (run-smoke.sh counts the frames between the commit and the marker key's echo: 0)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
mark settled
expect sess \$
sleep 12
mark idled
send h
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*h
send \x03
expect Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
